DocuAgentS sample-set work
==========================

This repository is a fork of the Invoice Extraction Benchmark
(https://github.com/DrewKraken/invoice-extraction-benchmark), pinned at commit
3f8864d0d96103a279b5320000c69a71068edd14. The upstream files are kept unchanged
except for the additions listed below.

Upstream material (unchanged, upstream licences retained)
---------------------------------------------------------

* Code in `generator/` and `scorer/`: MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 InvoiceParser Pro.
  The full text is in `LICENSE`, which this fork does not modify.
* Documents and answer keys in `corpus/` and `examples/`: Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0). The full text is in `DATA_LICENSE`.
  Credit: "InvoiceParser Pro, Invoice Extraction Benchmark v1",
  https://github.com/DrewKraken/invoice-extraction-benchmark
* The handwriting font (Windows Ink Free, `Inkfree.ttf`) is NOT redistributed
  here and is not part of this repository. Upstream records that the published
  handwritten documents were drawn with it.

Additions in this fork (new material only)
------------------------------------------

* New code — `docuagents_gen/` and `tests/test_upstream_compat.py`:
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 DocuAgentS contributors.
  This grant covers only the new files. It does not replace or extend the
  upstream MIT grant, and it does not apply to `generator/` or `scorer/`.
* New data — any sample documents, annotations, gold files or reports that
  DocuAgentS adds in later tasks under its own `samples/`, `reports/` and
  `gold/` directories: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
  This grant covers only new DocuAgentS data. It does not apply to the
  upstream `corpus/` or `examples/`, which stay under the upstream CC BY 4.0
  terms and attribution above.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

`requirements-dev.txt` pins every direct dependency; `environment.lock.json`
records the exact versions and their licences. Notable choices:

* `pypdfium2` (Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause) renders PDF pages. PyMuPDF is
  AGPL and is not used.
* `pdfplumber` (MIT) extracts PDF text and tables.
* `reportlab` (BSD-3-Clause) and `Pillow` (MIT-CMU/HPND) are the upstream
  generator's pinned dependencies.

No dependency is redistributed in this repository.

Attribution required when reusing the data
------------------------------------------

Any reuse of the upstream documents, answer keys or any DocuAgentS sample data
must keep the attribution above and state the licence (CC BY 4.0). Any reuse of
the code must keep the MIT copyright notice.
